1
00:00:03,690 --> 00:00:06,350
Hey, I read that someone invented a way

2
00:00:06,350 --> 00:00:08,860
to covert your footsteps into electromagnetic energy,

3
00:00:08,860 --> 00:00:10,960
so you can charge your cell phone while walking.

4
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:12,740
We had that idea years ago.

5
00:00:12,740 --> 00:00:14,090
How come we never did anything with it?

6
00:00:14,090 --> 00:00:16,540
Probably because we left the diagram of it in the restaurant,

7
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:19,160
and none of us wanted to walk back.

8
00:00:20,850 --> 00:00:23,820
I know the real reason you never made progress with that idea.

9
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:27,070
You thought of it September 22, 2007.

10
00:00:27,070 --> 00:00:29,510
Two days later, Penny moved in,

11
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:31,750
and so much blood rushed to your genitals,

12
00:00:31,750 --> 00:00:33,920
your brain became a ghost town.

13
00:00:35,810 --> 00:00:37,340
That's not what happened.

14
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:39,100
I remember it distinctly

15
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:41,580
because I had just composed my annual poem

16
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:44,390
commemorating the anniversary of Dr. Seuss's death.

17
00:00:44,390 --> 00:00:45,280
No one wants to hear it.

18
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:46,890
Why, die.

19
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:48,390
Why did he die?

20
00:00:48,390 --> 00:00:49,500
Old, told.

21
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:51,870
I was told he was old.

22
00:00:52,690 --> 00:00:55,250
Penny is not the reason I didn't pursue that idea.

23
00:00:55,250 --> 00:00:57,330
Oh, really? Since meeting her,

24
00:00:57,330 --> 00:00:59,860
what have been your greatest accomplishments?

25
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:00,710
Easy.

26
00:01:00,710 --> 00:01:02,520
Sleeping with Penny.

27
00:01:02,650 --> 00:01:05,310
Getting Penny to go back out with him after she dumped him.

28
00:01:05,310 --> 00:01:07,020
Tricking Penny into getting engaged.

29
00:01:07,020 --> 00:01:11,150
And a few weeks ago, he almost did a pull-up.

30
00:01:12,830 --> 00:01:15,440
I think someone owes me an apology.

31
00:01:16,380 --> 00:01:17,840
Well, don't feel bad.

32
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:19,460
I think we've all been distracted

33
00:01:19,460 --> 00:01:21,520
since the girls entered our lives.

34
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:23,130
You admit Amy's a distraction?

35
00:01:23,130 --> 00:01:24,730
Oh, very much so.

36
00:01:24,890 --> 00:01:27,670
Listen to this. This is from two days ago.

37
00:01:27,670 --> 00:01:30,720
"Hi. Hope you're having a good day."

38
00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:34,300
Who has time for this constant sexting?

39
00:01:34,970 --> 00:01:37,300
Well, maybe we have lost our focus.

40
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:41,050
It wouldn't kill us to get together and brainstorm ideas.

41
00:01:41,050 --> 00:01:43,340
Ooh, we could have one of those retreats.

42
00:01:43,340 --> 00:01:44,940
Like our own science retreat.

43
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:46,840
My cousin has a cabin out in the woods.

44
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:49,450
I'm not going to a cabin in the woods.

45
00:01:49,450 --> 00:01:52,770
Did you see the movie Cabin in the Woods?

46
00:01:52,770 --> 00:01:54,120
Then we'll go to a hotel.

47
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:58,690
A hotel? Did you see The Shining?

48
00:01:58,690 --> 00:01:59,860
We could go up to Big Bear

49
00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:00,950
and get a house on the lake.

50
00:02:00,950 --> 00:02:03,830
Did you see The Lake House?

51
00:02:03,830 --> 00:02:06,160
Nothing bad happens in The Lake House.

52
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:08,970
Yeah, well, no, not to them. To me.

53
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:11,120
Time traveling mailbox.

54
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:11,860
The only time that traveled

55
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:14,720
was an hour and half of my life down the toilet.

56
00:02:14,860 --> 00:02:16,660
Fine. Then we'll just stay here and do it.

57
00:02:16,660 --> 00:02:18,340
Well, you didn't suggest a beach house.

58
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:19,570
You would go to a beach house?

59
00:02:19,570 --> 00:02:22,540
Well, good Lord, no-- have you seen Jaws?

60
00:02:49,890 --> 00:02:51,190
So, the guys and I are talking about

61
00:02:51,190 --> 00:02:53,490
having kind of a science retreat this weekend.

62
00:02:53,490 --> 00:02:55,340
I just wanted to know if that's okay.

63
00:02:55,340 --> 00:02:57,250
You and I had talked about going to brunch on Sunday...

64
00:02:57,250 --> 00:02:58,260
Want to go to Vegas this weekend?

65
00:02:58,260 --> 00:02:59,560
Of course I do.

66
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:00,680
Bernadette?

67
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:01,970
Girl's weekend. Vegas. You in?

68
00:03:01,970 --> 00:03:03,770
- Hell, yeah! - Yes!

69
00:03:03,770 --> 00:03:05,590
- I'll check flights. - I'll check hotels.

70
00:03:05,590 --> 00:03:06,610
I'll check my underpants.

71
00:03:06,610 --> 00:03:08,790
I'm so excited, I think I peed.

72
00:03:17,630 --> 00:03:19,160
They seem okay with it.

73
