116
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:06,320
Okay, let's just skip all the inventions you can have sex with.

117
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:14,540
All right, no-- here we go:

118
00:05:14,540 --> 00:05:16,240
"Ergonomic heated seat cushion."

119
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:18,230
No, it vibrates. Keep going.

120
00:05:21,840 --> 00:05:23,940
You know, let's just come up with something new.

121
00:05:23,940 --> 00:05:26,170
You know, a number of significant innovations

122
00:05:26,170 --> 00:05:28,070
have been inspired by science fiction.

123
00:05:28,070 --> 00:05:31,450
The-the geosynchronous satellite from Arthur C. Clarke.

124
00:05:31,450 --> 00:05:34,210
The Motorola flip phone-- that came from Star Trek.

125
00:05:34,210 --> 00:05:36,610
Yeah, and I've long suspected that the idea

126
00:05:36,610 --> 00:05:38,750
of an African-American president was stolen

127
00:05:38,750 --> 00:05:42,100
from the movie Deep Impact.

128
00:05:43,530 --> 00:05:46,730
Hey, the future they show in Back to the Future II

129
00:05:46,730 --> 00:05:48,610
is only a year away.

130
00:05:48,610 --> 00:05:50,770
A lot of the things in that movie haven't been invented yet.

131
00:05:50,770 --> 00:05:51,950
How cool would that be

132
00:05:51,950 --> 00:05:53,520
if we could make one of those a reality?

133
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:55,330
If we could figure out the scientific basis

134
00:05:55,330 --> 00:05:56,760
for Marty's hover board,

135
00:05:56,760 --> 00:05:59,010
that would have universal application.

136
00:05:59,010 --> 00:06:01,180
Well, it's-it's possible at absolute zero,

137
00:06:01,180 --> 00:06:04,200
but we would have to remove the temperature restrictions.

138
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:05,650
Oh, I have an idea.

139
00:06:05,650 --> 00:06:06,960
I think I have the same one.

140
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:09,280
We got to watch Back to the Future II!

141
00:06:11,140 --> 00:06:13,490
I'll make the popcorn.

142
00:06:15,690 --> 00:06:17,470
So, where should we go first?

143
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,920
There's a cover band in the lounge.

144
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:22,120
- Nah. - But they play Barry Manilow.

145
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:25,940
- No. - But they're called "Fairly Manilow."

146
00:06:27,170 --> 00:06:28,180
Oh. Okay.

147
00:06:28,180 --> 00:06:29,990
- Great! - No!

148
00:06:31,160 --> 00:06:32,220
Well, what do you want to do?

149
00:06:32,220 --> 00:06:33,780
Well, we're in Vegas.

150
00:06:33,780 --> 00:06:36,380
I want to go downstairs, get a bucket of margaritas,

151
00:06:36,380 --> 00:06:38,760
dance until I vomit all over a roulette wheel

152
00:06:38,760 --> 00:06:40,520
and watch it go everywhere.

153
00:06:41,450 --> 00:06:43,030
What if we don't want to vomit?

154
00:06:43,030 --> 00:06:45,690
Oh, you will. That's why they give you the bucket.

155
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:48,800
What?

156
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:50,300
It's my boss.

157
00:06:50,300 --> 00:06:52,470
They moved my field ride up to Monday.

158
00:06:52,470 --> 00:06:53,580
What does that mean?

159
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:55,360
It means instead of having a week to study,

160
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:56,850
I only have two days.

161
00:06:56,850 --> 00:06:58,020
That sucks.

162
00:06:58,020 --> 00:06:59,720
Can you start in the morning?

163
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:01,460
Uh, it's kind of a lot.

164
00:07:01,460 --> 00:07:02,610
You know, let me do a little tonight,

165
00:07:02,610 --> 00:07:04,050
and I'll catch up with you guys later.

166
00:07:04,050 --> 00:07:06,190
- You sure? - Yeah, it's okay. Go ahead.

167
00:07:08,370 --> 00:07:10,340
So, um, now that Penny's not coming...

168
00:07:10,340 --> 00:07:12,450
- We're not seeing Fairly Manilow. - Okay.

169
00:07:19,870 --> 00:07:21,640
Hold on. Pause.

170
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:24,180
Something doesn't make sense. Look...

171
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:28,640
In 2015, Biff steals the sports almanac

172
00:07:28,640 --> 00:07:32,420
and takes the time machine back to 1955,

173
00:07:32,420 --> 00:07:34,080
to give it to his younger self.

174
00:07:34,080 --> 00:07:37,110
But as soon as he does that, he changes the future,

175
00:07:37,110 --> 00:07:39,360
so the 2015 he returns to would be

176
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:43,920
a different 2015, not the 2015 that Marty and Doc were in.

177
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:48,850
This is Hot Tub Time Machine all over again.

178
00:07:49,620 --> 00:07:51,850
If future Biff goes back to 2015

179
00:07:51,850 --> 00:07:53,960
right after he gives young Biff the almanac,

180
00:07:53,960 --> 00:07:57,050
he could get back to the 2015 with Marty and Doc in it.

181
00:07:57,050 --> 00:07:59,950
Because it wasn't until his 21st birthday

182
00:07:59,950 --> 00:08:03,010
that 1955 Biff placed his first bet.

183
00:08:03,010 --> 00:08:03,830
Wait. Whoa, whoa.

184
00:08:03,830 --> 00:08:05,460
Is "placed" right?

185
00:08:05,460 --> 00:08:06,290
What do you mean?

186
00:08:06,290 --> 00:08:08,450
Is "placed" the right tense

187
00:08:08,450 --> 00:08:10,530
for something that would have happened in the future

188
00:08:10,530 --> 00:08:13,950
of a past that was affected by something from the future?

189
00:08:15,370 --> 00:08:17,870
Had will have placed?

190
00:08:17,870 --> 00:08:20,040
That's my boy.

191
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:24,920
Okay, so, it wasn't until his 21st birthday

192
00:08:24,920 --> 00:08:27,360
that Biff had will have placed his first bet

193
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:28,520
and made his millions.

194
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:30,670
That's when he altered the timeline.

195
00:08:30,670 --> 00:08:34,010
Yeah, but he had will haven't placed it!

196
00:08:36,210 --> 00:08:37,900
What?!

197
00:08:38,370 --> 00:08:39,980
Unlike Hot Tub Time Machine,

198
00:08:39,980 --> 00:08:41,880
this couldn't be more simple.

199
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:44,440
When Biff gets the almanac in 1955,

200
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:47,060
the alternate future he creates isn't the one

201
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:49,580
in which Marty and Doc Brown ever use the time machine

202
00:08:49,580 --> 00:08:51,090
to travel to 2015.

203
00:08:51,090 --> 00:08:51,940
Therefore,

204
00:08:51,940 --> 00:08:53,190
in the new timeline,

205
00:08:53,190 --> 00:08:55,460
Marty and Doc never brought the time machine...

206
00:08:55,460 --> 00:08:56,310
W-Wait.

207
00:08:56,310 --> 00:08:57,960
Is "brought" right?

208
00:09:02,260 --> 00:09:06,370
Marty and Doc never had have had brought?

209
00:09:07,660 --> 00:09:09,630
I don't know. You did it to me.

210
00:09:11,460 --> 00:09:12,580
Oh, I'm going with it.

211
00:09:12,580 --> 00:09:14,850
Marty and Doc never had have had brought

212
00:09:14,850 --> 00:09:16,830
the time machine to 2015.

213
00:09:16,830 --> 00:09:19,750
That means 2015 Biff could also

214
00:09:19,750 --> 00:09:23,850
not had have had brought the almanac to 1955 Biff.

215
00:09:23,850 --> 00:09:28,340
Therefore, the timeline in which 1955 Biff gets the almanac

216
00:09:28,340 --> 00:09:29,670
is also the timeline

217
00:09:29,670 --> 00:09:32,730
in which 1955 Biff never gets the almanac.

218
00:09:32,730 --> 00:09:34,310
And not just "never gets."

219
00:09:34,310 --> 00:09:35,850
Never have, never hasn't,

220
00:09:35,850 --> 00:09:38,310
never had have hasn't.

221
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:45,190
He's right.

222
00:09:46,910 --> 00:09:49,540
Also, what kind of name is Biff?

223
00:09:49,540 --> 00:09:52,540
Sounds like when you pop open a can of Pillsbury dough.

224
00:09:53,220 --> 00:09:54,600
Biff.

225
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:59,270
Oh, that stuff is so good wrapped around cocktail weenies.

226
00:09:59,270 --> 00:09:59,890
Guys...

227
00:09:59,890 --> 00:10:01,440
Do you know that the word "Wiener"

228
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:04,130
comes from the German name of the Austrian capital Vienna,

229
00:10:04,130 --> 00:10:05,050
or "Wien"?

230
00:10:05,050 --> 00:10:06,290
Do you know if you look at Austria on a map

231
00:10:06,290 --> 00:10:08,130
it actually looks like a wiener?

232
00:10:09,300 --> 00:10:10,350
Guys, what are we doing?

233
00:10:10,350 --> 00:10:11,530
W-We sent the girls away

234
